  "terrainName": "basic-desert",
  "description": "What: CE-4649 (bows BW-11) - on basic-desert three Archers (Friend, 80/110/140,100) each shoot 5 arrows at the face centre of an archery target prop 30 m north (TKB 2015, a straw boss with a 10-ring face). Judge: (1) 15 arrows are fired (2) every arrow ends in a target (Hit) or the ground (StoppedByTerrain). Each archer's ArcheryScore measure sums the rings (ArcheryScoring.RingAt) of his arrows that strike a target, under a Points root; a Best names the top archer. Judge: (3) every archer's ArcheryScore is above 0. The Points root and the Best are authored but NOT judged: with the parallel or threaded kernel on, a rule created at load never sees its children (CE-4649 note), so they only read right under HROT_PARALLEL_SIM=0 HROT_THREADED_KERNEL=0. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh bw-archery-contest"
 },
